    "intro_html":  "Turkey divan is a church potluck legend, and the thing that makes it a legend is the curry powder. Just a little, stirred into a cream sauce, and suddenly the whole casserole tastes like somebody knew what they were doing. Turkey, broccoli, and rice under a buttered crumb crust, baked until the top crackles. Each serving comes to \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
